On Wednesday, March 02, 2016 11:41:58 Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
> And, would "ya" in "yard" suffice?

"ya" in "yard" is good for "ia", unless you r-color the vowel. There are too 
many variations in the pronunciation of vowels in English. I think it's better 
to explain the Lojban vowels in terms of Spanish, except "y". But there are a 
few Spanish speakers who pronounce vowels differently (I've read that they 
change vowel quality in front of /s/, and I've heard someone talk like that, 
but I haven't analyzed her speech to figure out exactly what she's doing).

